---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import SampleComponent from "@components/SampleComponent.astro";
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import AstroLogo from "@assets/images/astro-logo-light-gradient.png";
import { Content as SampleMarkdown } from "@content/sample-markdown.md";
import { Assets } from "astro:assets";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Logo from './MainLogo.svg';

import ImagePopout from "@components/ImagePopout.astro";


import Nav from "@components/Nav.astro"
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro"
import ProjectButton from "@components/ProjectButton.astro";

---

<Layout title="Esports Visualized">
  <Nav />
  <div style=" margin: 100px; "></div>
  <Container>
    <div class="about">
        <Image src={Logo} alt="logo for Esports Visualized" width={800} />
        <h1>About the Project</h1>
        <p>
          My name is Tyler Boggi and I have been designing for the Esports space for 3 years now from clubs, to organizations, and beyond.
          It’s a pleasure to be able to showcase everything that I’ve learned here and then some. With this project my goal is to get people
          interested in the scene of Esports and its flourishing and truly unique design opportunities! 
        </p>
        <p>
          Many of you may be asking, what is Esports? Esports is a colloquial term for competitive gaming, covering several genres of game.
          With a projected 640 million viewers in 2025, the scene has been growing rapidly. There are hundreds of thousands of competitors
          across over 150+ different games. This has led to a community of richly creative people from all different backgrounds.
        </p>
        <p>
          I would classify three things that make Esports unique. Firstly, Esports is accessible, with the only requirements being the game,
          the console, and a controller. This means that Esports transcends the physical and social boundaries that can often hold
          traditional sports back. Second, is the community it provides, which is so large expanding through so many different games
          that you’re bound to find your people. Lastly, is innovation, with so many diverse and passionate voices in the community,
          creativity thrives here in so many different forms.
        </p>
        <p>
          Esports Visualized is a project that focuses on how graphic design takes shape in the context of the Esports community.
          This project highlights a few different specific fields of graphic design relevant to Esports and focuses on how they are
          different or unique when being made for Esports. These are done in the form of case studies, where I discuss the aspect of
          design itself and how it differs when applied to Esports but take it one step further and apply it myself to give a
          visual demonstration of what is discussed in the case study. These will all be real and applied designs made for a
          purpose in order to give an accurate depiction of what it is like to design for Esports and the unique challenges that come with it!
        </p>
        <p>
          If you’d like to learn more on how you can start playing your favorite games competitively or just join the scene for the enjoyment
          of all the unique opportunities and graphic design that goes on then contact me! I hope you enjoy the project and that it
          gets you to look at Esports graphic design in a new light!
        </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
</script>

<style>
  /*About Section*/
  .about{
    display: flex;
    flex-flow: column nowrap;
    height: fit-content;
    gap: 30px;
    font-size: 18pt;
    padding: 20px;
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 600px){
    .about{
      padding: 0px;
      font-size: 12pt;
    }
  }
</style>